# Trivy ignore list for the CRITICAL-blocking scan in ci-security.yml
# (Container image scan (Trivy, CRITICAL, blocking)).
#
# Every entry here is an accepted, documented exception, not a blanket
# severity downgrade. The full report-only scan in the same workflow still
# shows these (and every HIGH finding) on every run, so they stay visible.
# Review this file every phase per spec §10's threat-model rule, and remove
# an entry the moment a real fix is available.

# zlib: integer overflow and resultant heap-based buffer overflow in
# inflate() via a large gzip header extra field. Debian marks this
# "will_not_fix" for the zlib1g package shipped in the python/node slim
# base images used here (bookworm/trixie) - there is no patched Debian
# package version to upgrade to. Upstream zlib considers it low-risk
# outside of attacker-controlled gzip headers passed to inflate(), which
# this codebase does not do directly.
CVE-2023-45853
